  "text:You explored At the Little Shop. Say the English sentence and show what it means.": "/audio/a3745e47c94b329bb9305b41.mp3",
  "text:The answer is 8. Thank you for trying. Add five taka for the mango and three taka for the banana. The total is eight taka.": "/audio/be6726b2d6bdb0d2f4693599.mp3",
  "text:Set the playtime clock to three o’clock.": "/audio/e3ca0f5d42020af56d1b7a2e.mp3",
  "text:The answer is ৳5. The mango costs five taka.": "/audio/63ca92994112363e145ac3d1.mp3",
  "text:A new clock. What time is it?": "/audio/dd6bb1445a416a0e6792b656.mp3",
  "text:It is six o’clock.": "/audio/b7005f8f3bee4070e05ecb7a.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Three o’clock. Thank you for trying. The short hand points to three. The long hand points to twelve.": "/audio/6d44a945b512ef6526bf9f2e.mp3",
  "text:The answer is six o’clock. It is six o’clock.": "/audio/8a28db81630902ffdcf49062.mp3",
  "text:Give the bird three stickers and the flower two.": "/audio/0b97c0a85278c7454e308e85.mp3",
  "text:You explored The Playtime Clock. Say the English sentence and show what it means.": "/audio/e0072d3c087af9a4c77ca8dd.mp3",
  "text:Which row has the most stickers?": "/audio/bb1c1be9f39d04b3d054f8af.mp3",
  "text:The answer is 1. Thank you for trying. Match two stickers in each row. The bird has one extra sticker.": "/audio/bc45337ec6b56a84b365a633.mp3",
  "text:The bird has three stickers. The flower has two stickers.": "/audio/72b910c4e27f173cf5b06822.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Bird. Thank you for trying. Count three stickers for the bird and two for the flower. The bird has more.": "/audio/a20699fb750c8d40666b75c0.mp3",
  "text:Count both rows. Three is more than two.": "/audio/371f0515f3267560c3506a3a.mp3",
  "text:The flower row has three. The bird row has two.": "/audio/6ad80724c7d4253c492c3114.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Flower. Count both rows. Three is more than two.": "/audio/bf72dcd21ae582c5332711a3.mp3",
  "text:You explored The Sticker Chart. Say the English sentence and show what it means.": "/audio/7e8e939a39726bfbbe1de1d2.mp3",
  "text:You explored Plants Need Sunlight. Come back and test what you remember.": "/audio/4558eb40a126f4fe718bd858.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Grass in sunlight. Thank you for trying. The green grass had sunlight. The covered grass became pale over several days.": "/audio/28704ab42798abeed1a176e1.mp3",
  "text:Both patches get the same care. Let several days pass, then uncover the grass.": "/audio/f69325cd1409fad9988c0895.mp3",
  "text:Explore how water travels. Follow our model step by step.": "/audio/347a6d776a958bbb99175876.mp3",
  "text:The answer is The Sun. Thank you for trying. Look at the sunlight warming the river.": "/audio/a8de715a161f789642576e6f.mp3",
  "text:Warming, rising vapour, cooling cloud drops, then rain.": "/audio/00dfe9ab3f16a0fc08d093ce.mp3",
  "text:Put the water-cycle stages in order.": "/audio/d2e0099bc7b5086dda9bb10d.mp3",
  "text:Tap a body helper to find its job.": "/audio/e5b6687e6fba85b3e8539bb1.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Lungs. Thank you for trying. Find the two blue lungs in the chest. They help us breathe.": "/audio/cb1a81aa181abd85fbad2477.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Rain. Thank you for trying. The tiny cloud drops join into larger drops that fall as rain.": "/audio/f2790cf36ed8f37de742bdef.mp3",
  "text:You explored Where Does Rain Come From?. Come back and test what you remember.": "/audio/cd2f6dfb41d49554649e78ad.mp3",
  "text:The brain helps us think and move.": "/audio/018798f034b784881590e73b.mp3",
  "text:Which helper helps us think and move?": "/audio/2018574fd120b798b27ee5f3.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Heart. Thank you for trying. The heart is the pump. It moves blood around the body.": "/audio/84ebb783310173c50f5f9430.mp3",
  "text:The answer is brain. The brain helps us think and move.": "/audio/7d84aeaeb732f450a863ee15.mp3",
  "text:Explore with our senses.": "/audio/020c34899f5eb805ab78ec04.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Ears. Thank you for trying. The bell makes a sound. Our ears help us hear it.": "/audio/a904d5cebb74acc8a95908fd.mp3",
  "text:You explored Our Body Helpers. Come back and test what you remember.": "/audio/03bc123e36fe9083d652b08d.mp3",
  "text:Which body part helps us hear?": "/audio/4d03da5de50a1af9676f10b9.mp3",
  "text:Which body part helps us smell?": "/audio/f5f196c08b1f02a27f80c471.mp3",
  "text:The answer is ears. We hear with our ears.": "/audio/76832809864d235065f89bd5.mp3",
  "text:The answer is nose. We smell with our nose.": "/audio/446a76e0c22055d553dd1a8c.mp3",
  "text:Which body part helps us taste?": "/audio/c179b22213aeb2cf007a2cbc.mp3",
  "text:We touch with our skin.": "/audio/5987918820fe41abbca66beb.mp3",
  "text:Which body part helps us touch?": "/audio/22bace23c707c21676311408.mp3",
  "text:The answer is tongue. We taste with our tongue.": "/audio/01e1c5cd374e00c7cd6fcdc6.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Tongue. Thank you for trying. The tongue helps us taste the apple. The nose helps us smell.": "/audio/c071d4c952d722fe970cffb4.mp3",
  "text:You explored Our Five Senses. Come back and test what you remember.": "/audio/c14e4c807b5a8e5c9494ff8b.mp3",
  "text:Match these animals to places shown in this story.": "/audio/06497b1f4b9b74afadb40242.mp3",
  "text:The answer is skin. We touch with our skin.": "/audio/9384f09e12d798e4eaabe35e.mp3",
  "text:Turn Earth. Watch our marked place move into night.": "/audio/956972ab3ca232cc3e09b468.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Farm. Thank you for trying. Remember the cow near the barn. We showed a farm.": "/audio/7889d6686c9ee36f872147b4.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Pond. Thank you for trying. Remember the frog beside the water. Its home in our story is the pond.": "/audio/490cf1de23d0730ab7655fc8.mp3",
  "text:You explored Animal Homes. Come back and test what you remember.": "/audio/dfb5c25e3092f1e3c883b20a.mp3",
  "text:You explored Day and Night. Come back and test what you remember.": "/audio/09efa02d65dd0e6f64e105f5.mp3",
  "text:Predict, then put the object in the water.": "/audio/316ca7b6ad150388dc772055.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Facing the Sun. Thank you for trying. The Sun lights the side facing it. The other side is dark.": "/audio/c02ebd654d7adda9d59e6d58.mp3",
  "text:Which tested object sank?": "/audio/6ced6d11656d207dc76cbc59.mp3",
  "text:The solid steel key sank.": "/audio/c7ac66a4aa71db24a21dd8f5.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Wooden block. Thank you for trying. The wooden block stayed at the water surface. The solid steel key went down.": "/audio/39b55dd8984edb3855359408.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Steel key. Thank you for trying. Look at the key at the bottom of the water.": "/audio/6543a8eed6cf3fb343498aa8.mp3",
  "text:Move the toy away. Pull the wagon closer.": "/audio/126b8ce64b187e2845b16d96.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Steel key. The solid steel key sank.": "/audio/004dd0dbce7f32c276740ced.mp3",
  "text:You explored Float or Sink?. Come back and test what you remember.": "/audio/89c995c3ca2503127a77c3c2.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Pulling the wagon. Thank you for trying. Look at the rope pulling the wagon toward the child.": "/audio/d8e7fb5d0dfb61e11d9f8a17.mp3",
  "text:You explored Push and Pull. Come back and test what you remember.": "/audio/d2a5c6fd9d7b6148b790a12f.mp3",
  "text:Predict, then test each object with the magnet.": "/audio/9f7abe15322517e769cde095.mp3",
  "text:You explored A Magnet Can Pull. Come back and test what you remember.": "/audio/877462cbd367796f928cd5d2.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Aluminium foil. Thank you for trying. The foil is metal, but this ordinary magnet did not pull it.": "/audio/093272556302ccbf1c22529b.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Pushing the toy. Thank you for trying. A push moves the toy away from the child. A pull brings the wagon closer.": "/audio/0c9de7cf430a047a8a63d823.mp3",
  "text:The answer is Steel paper clip. Thank you for trying. This plain steel clip is magnetic. The wood and aluminium foil did not move.": "/audio/e38cada231783d87b1727e3d.mp3",
  "text:Turn the lamp on. Then turn it off.": "/audio/ab7e194edd260b1576e84b2b.mp3",
  "text:You matched A with a.": "/audio/4134f6da42e2f35079911975.mp3",
